   </table>\n            <p style=\"margin: 10px 0 0 0; font-size: 12px; color: #374151; line-height: 1.5;\">💡 <strong>NVDA earnings Aug 26</strong> — the AI capex-to-NVDA-revenue transmission you've been reading about. Say <code>analyze NVDA</code> for the full setup if you want to look at a pre-earnings position.</p>\n            <p style=\"margin: 6px 0 0 0; font-size: 12px; color: #374151; line-height: 1.5;\">💡 <strong>AVGO earnings Sep 3</strong> — say <code>analyze AVGO</code> for the full setup.</p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- PENDING WATCHLIST -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 20px 24px 0 24px;\">\n            <table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"background-color: #1a1400; border-left: 3px solid #f59e0b; border-radius: 6px;\">\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"padding: 16px 18px;\">\n                  <p style=\"margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: #f59e0b;\">⏳ Pending Watchlist</p>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 13px; color: #e5e7eb; line-height: 1.6;\">No active watchlist candidates right now. The 5 entries in portfolio.json (IQV, CELC, CAPR, VRDN, VERA) are all archived — closed positions from the binary-catalyst era, kept for the trade log. New-candidate discovery isn't part of this daily routine; run <code>stock-finder</code> when you want fresh ideas to screen against your cash.</p>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- CASH DEPLOYMENT -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 20px 24px 0 24px;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600;\">💵 Cash Deployment</p>\n            <table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"background-color: #eff6ff; border: 1px solid #bfdbfe; border-radius: 8px;\">\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"padding: 14px 16px; font-size: 13px; color: #1e3a8a; line-height: 1.6;\">\n                  <strong>Hold off.</strong> $542.01 shown available would normally clear the $30 deployment minimum easily, but that figure is 11 days stale and the GOOG order above may have already committed ~$104 of it to an unprotected position. Reconcile IBKR first — confirm actual cash and actual holdings — before sizing anything new. Once confirmed: no fresh discovery candidate is generated automatically here, run <code>stock-finder</code> when there's cash to deploy and you want new ideas.\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- ROTATION -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 20px 24px 0 24px;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 12px; color: #9ca3af;\">🔄 Rotation suggestions: N/A — no open positions to rotate.</p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- IBKR INTELLIGENCE -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 24px 0 24px;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 11px; color: #9ca3af;\">📊 IBKR Intelligence — not available in routine mode. Trigger daily check in chat for full broker analytics.</p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- EDUCATION -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 20px 24px 24px 24px;\">\n            <table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"background-color: #f1f5f9; border-radius: 8px;\">\n              <tr>\n                <td style=\"padding: 20px 24px;\">\n                  <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 11px; color: #475569; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;\">📚 Today you learned</p>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 8px 0 0 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a;\">Pattern Day Trader (PDT) Rule</p>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 12px 0 0 0; font-size: 13px; color: #1e293b; line-height: 1.7;\">\n                    Forex has no equivalent of this. In a US margin account under $25k equity — yours is ~$542 — FINRA flags you as a Pattern Day Trader the moment you execute 4+ day trades (buy and sell the same ticker same session) within any rolling 5 business-day window. Once flagged, the broker restricts you to closing-only trades until you either deposit up to $25k or the flag ages off. Your CELC round trip (bought and sold same day, Jul 15) counts as one day trade. Your \"days not weeks\" momentum strategy is built for holds of a day or more, which mostly keeps you clear — but a fast stop-out same day as entry, twice more in a rolling week, and IBKR locks you out of new entries regardless of how good the next setup looks. Track same-day round trips mentally; it's a hard broker-side wall, not a risk-management choice you get to override.\n                  </p>\n                  <p style=\"margin: 12px 0 0 0; font-size: 12px; color: #475569; font-style: italic;\">\n                    Also today: <strong>Marketable limit order</strong> — a buy limit set at or above the current ask (or sell limit at/below the current bid) that executes immediately like a market order but still caps your fill price; useful for illiquid small-caps where a plain market order risks a bad print.\n                  </p>\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            </table>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <!-- FOOTER -->\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 16px 24px 24px 24px; border-top: 1px solid #f3f4f6;\">\n            <p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 10px; color: #9ca3af; line-height: 1.5;\">\n              Research output, not financial advice. Past performance does not guarantee future results.\n              Verify halal compliance quarterly on Zoya or Musaffa. Prices: web search (Yahoo Finance/Stooq JSON APIs blocked by network egress proxy this session, as they were yesterday — GOOG/AXTI/SPXC figures are directional, not exact). Generated Sunday 2026-08-16, Kuwait time.\n            </p>\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n\n      </table>\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n"}